<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaogong ji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">Warring States period</span> · Also known as Record of Trades, Artificers' Record</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kaogong ji is an ancient Chinese technical treatise on crafts, preserved as the last section of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rites-of-zhou">Rites of Zhou</a> in place of a lost chapter. It describes some thirty trades, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> building, bronze casting with set alloy proportions, weapon making and the plan of an ideal royal capital. Probably compiled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a>, it is often thought to come from the State of Qi.</p></div>
